**Placement rationale.**

- `sakg/schema/` — not `spec/`, not `conformance/`. The schema is SAKG-side runtime data
  loaded by `sakg/store.py` and `sakg/ingest.py`; the backlog's `trust_zone` note places
  all `sakg/` in Zone 2 and states the dependency arrow is one-way (PAEOS never imports
  `sakg`). Putting the schema in `sakg/` keeps that arrow intact.
- **No `sakg/__init__.py` at this node.** I-STORE owns `pyproject` package registration
  (`backlog/SAKG-1-backlog.yaml`, I-STORE deliverables). F-ENVELOPE ships a data directory
  only, so it can land before `sakg` is an importable package. Test loading is by path
  (`pathlib`), matching the accept command's own `pathlib.Path(...).read_text()`.
- `tests/sakg/fixtures/envelope/{valid,invalid}/` must be **flat** — the accept command
  globs `valid/*.json` at exactly one level; a subdirectory would silently not be counted.
- `manifest.json` sits at `fixtures/envelope/`, **one level above** `valid/` and
  `invalid/`, so it can never be miscounted by the accept globs.

**No orphan:** every new file is reachable — the schema and both fixture trees are read by
`test_envelope_schema.py`; the manifest is the index that makes the read exhaustive.

