## §3 Data flow

```
 PAEOS goal seals at L16
        │  (post-seal, one-way, pull-based — §6.1)
        ▼
 L15 outbox bundle  ──validated against──▶  envelope.schema.json#/$defs/IngestNode
        │                                     confidence ABSENT · status = candidate
        ▼
 sakg ingest (I-INGEST)
        │  derives confidence · assigns valid_from · keeps namespace = producing project
        ▼
 StoredNode  ──validated against──▶  envelope.schema.json#   (root = StoredNode)
        │
        ├──▶ I-STORE persistence  (append-only; supersession only)
        └──▶ I-PROJ projection: `summary` is the SUMMARY-tier unit; filters read
             `status`, `confidence`, `valid_from`/`valid_until` (§5.1)
```

**Element-by-element, produced and consumed** (no unconsumed field):

| Field | Produced by | Consumed by |
|---|---|---|
| `id`, `type`, `namespace` | emission (`F-BUNDLE`) | store keying, namespace isolation (Ω5), edge endpoints (§4.4) |
| `facets` | emission + extension registration | type-specific readers; `I-TRADEOFF`, `I-TRAVERSE` |
| `label`, `summary` | emission | projection response `node_summary` (§5.1) — `summary` is the token-budget unit (Ω3/FPL-4) |
| `provenance.*` | emission | consumer re-verification (FPL-7); `trust: untrusted` tagging (§3.3.2) |
| `evidence` | emission (refs only) | promotion guard C1; `why` path construction (§5.1 rule 2) |
| `status` | ingest (`candidate`) then store transitions | projection `status` filter, default `[canonical]` (§5.1 rule 4) |
| `confidence` | **store, derived** (never emission) | projection `min_confidence` filter; confidence-collapse degradation (§7) |
| `valid_from` / `valid_until` | ingest / transition | `as_of` time-travel (§5.1) |
| `falsifier` | emission | refutation watch → status `refuted` (Ω4) |
| `coordinates` | emission | cross-domain retrieval, `analogous_to` neighbours (✓8, ✓9) |

**Fixture-corpus flow** (the second product of this node):

```
F-ENVELOPE valid/*    ─▶ I-STORE round-trip inputs ─▶ T-ROUNDTRIP loss-ratio check
F-ENVELOPE invalid/*  ─▶ I-INGEST rejection corpus (must reject every one)
F-ENVELOPE manifest   ─▶ the contract both of the above index against
envelope.schema.json  ─▶ F-BUNDLE `$ref`s #/$defs/IngestNode
```

**Cross-file `$ref` hand-off.** `$id` is `sakg://schema/envelope/1.0.0` — an opaque URI a
validator cannot fetch. F-BUNDLE must therefore build an explicit `referencing.Registry`
mapping that `$id` to the loaded envelope schema before compiling `bundle.schema.json`.
Recorded here so F-BUNDLE does not discover it as a defect (§13 hand-off item 6).

