## §7 Test module design — `tests/sakg/test_envelope_schema.py`

Requires `tests/sakg/__init__.py` (every existing `tests/*` subpackage has one).

| Test | Assertion | Why it exists |
|---|---|---|
| `test_schema_is_valid_draft_2020_12` | `Draft202012Validator.check_schema(schema)` | A malformed schema otherwise vacuously "accepts" everything |
| `test_manifest_is_bijective_with_disk` | every file in `valid/` ∪ `invalid/` has exactly one manifest entry and vice versa | an unindexed fixture is an untested fixture |
| `test_valid_fixtures_validate` | parametrized: each valid fixture validates against its declared profile pointer with zero errors | positive coverage |
| `test_invalid_fixtures_are_rejected_for_the_declared_reason` | parametrized: `iter_errors` is non-empty **and** contains an error whose `validator` == `violates.keyword` and whose `absolute_path` == `violates.instance_path` | **the important one** — rejection for the right reason, not by accident |
| `test_every_envelope_field_is_covered` | every field name in §2.2 appears in ≥1 valid fixture, and has ≥1 I-A/I-B omission fixture | "exercising every field" |
| `test_every_status_value_is_covered` | all four `status` values appear in the valid corpus | "every status value" |
| `test_every_node_type_is_covered` | all twelve §4.3 types appear in the valid corpus (⇒ all twelve C4 branches fire) | dead-branch detection |
| `test_every_invariant_has_an_invalid_fixture` | `INV-1 … INV-10` each appear in ≥1 `violates.id` | "every §4.2 invariant violation" |
| `test_corpus_floors` | `len(valid) >= 12` and `len(invalid) >= 8` | mirrors accept commands 3 and 4 inside pytest, so regression is caught by `pytest` alone |
| `test_single_defect_rule` | each invalid entry's `base` exists in the valid corpus and differs by exactly one JSON-pointer mutation | enforces §6.2's single-defect rule |

**Validator dependency.** `jsonschema` **4.26.0** is present in `uv.lock` and imports
today with `Draft202012Validator` — but only as a *transitive* dependency of `mcp`. A test
that depends on an undeclared transitive package is a latent breakage the moment `mcp`'s
dependency graph changes. IMPLEMENT should add `jsonschema>=4.26` to
`[dependency-groups].dev` in `pyproject.toml`. That key is disjoint from
`[tool.hatch.build.targets.wheel].packages`, which I-STORE owns, so there is no
merge-conflict surface. **The test must import `jsonschema` unconditionally** — an
`importorskip` would let `pytest -q` exit 0 with the entire suite skipped, turning accept
command 2 into theater.

