## §8 Frozen decisions register

These are the choices §4.2 leaves open. Each is a *freeze*, and freezing is irreversible —
which is precisely why F-ENVELOPE is a `fable` node. Each carries an escalation path.

| id | Decision | Rationale | If contested |
|---|---|---|---|
| **D-1** | Two profiles (`StoredNode` / `IngestNode`) in one file | The only way "authored confidence" becomes mechanically detectable; also gives F-BUNDLE a stable `$ref` target | Alternative — a separate `ingest.schema.json` — duplicates the field table and invites drift. Rejected. |
| **D-2** | `valid_until` and `falsifier` are **required-and-nullable**, not optional | Removes the absent/open ambiguity; Δ3 demands mechanical checkability | Founder/CIA may relax to optional; costs one invalid fixture each. |
| **D-3** | `evidence` is an array of **EvidenceRef node id URIs**, not inline objects | §3.2.3 / §3.3.3 "references only, never copies"; makes INV-7 structural and pre-satisfies F-BUNDLE's "forbids inline evidence payloads" | §4.2's `[EvidenceRef]` also admits an embedded-object reading. If chosen instead, INV-7 must move to §5.2 with an owner. |
| **D-4** | Pinned-ULID suffix block `E01`–`E99` for SAKG envelope fixtures | Determinism (SC-10 discipline); `E` verified unallocated in the Wave-0 table | Becomes a SAKG-1 SC entry if the CIA wants one allocation table across both backlogs. |
| **D-5** | Adopt SC-02 (hash) and SC-04 (timestamp) forms verbatim | Lexical comparability across the §6.1b emission boundary | Could be re-pinned per-SAKG; divergence would cost a translation layer at ingest. |
| **D-6** | `confidence` bounded to `[0, 1]` | §4.2 says only `float`; an unbounded confidence is unfilterable by `min_confidence` (§5.1) and the corpus norm is a probability (ADR-011's "confidence >75%") | Drop the bound and delete one I-D fixture. Recommended to keep. |
| **D-7** | `label` gets `minLength: 1` but **no** upper bound | `summary` is the projection unit and carries the spec's only length bound (280). Inventing a `label` ceiling would add a constraint §4.2 does not state | — |
| **D-8** | Facet keys must be namespaced (≥2 dotted segments) | §4.3: new facets require *namespace registration*; a lexical namespace requirement is the checkable shadow of that rule | Relax to any key; INV-10 then moves to §5.2. |

