## §10 Perspectives covered (L09 multi-perspective critique — all seven)

- **Builder.** The enumeration rules (§6.1, §6.2) are mechanical; the field table (§2.2)
  and lexical forms (§2.3) are transcribable without interpretation; the test set (§7) is
  fully specified. No judgment call is left to IMPLEMENT. ✔
- **Architect.** The envelope is the ECS `Entity` (✓7); facets are the only extension
  surface (Δ1's extension path preserved); the type set is closed (Δ4). The schema
  encodes §4.2 and nothing more — every constraint beyond the spec text is registered as
  an explicit freeze in §8, not smuggled in. ✔
- **Risk Officer.** The high-severity risk is **freezing the wrong contract**: F-ENVELOPE
  is a DAG root and four nodes depend on it. Mitigated by (a) the §8 register making every
  discretionary choice reversible-by-decision rather than buried, (b) §11 routing new
  ambiguities out instead of resolving them, (c) `$id` version `1.0.0` making a future
  break explicit. Residual: an over-constrained schema (D-2, D-6, D-8) could reject a
  legitimate future node — cheap to relax, expensive to tighten later, so the direction of
  the error is the safe one. ✔
- **Performance.** The schema is compiled once and reused; `$defs` reuse keeps `IngestNode`
  from duplicating the field table. Twelve C4 `if/then` branches are O(12) per document
  and only one can match. `summary`'s 280-char ceiling is what makes the FPL-4 token budget
  computable at projection time. ✔
- **Security.** This is SAKG's poisoning surface (Ω6). `additionalProperties: false` at
  root and in `provenance` blocks field-injection; INV-2 closes the ×5 statistical-promotion
  attack (PAEOS-7.5 T3e) *structurally* rather than by policy; INV-7 prevents an ingest
  path from smuggling an inline payload past the reference-only rule; `namespace` is a
  required, lexically constrained field so isolation (Ω5) has something to key on.
  Non-authority is unaffected — the schema grants no capability and mints no evidence
  (§3.3.3). ✔
- **Replay.** Every fixture is a pinned literal: fixed ULIDs, fixed SC-04 timestamps, fixed
  SC-02 hashes, nothing computed at test time. The corpus is byte-reproducible, so
  `T-ROUNDTRIP`'s loss ratio is measured against a stable target. ✔
- **Maintainer.** One file, one manifest, two flat fixture directories. The manifest↔disk
  bijection test means a fixture cannot be added without being indexed or deleted without
  being noticed. `violates` makes each invalid fixture self-documenting. The §5.2 table
  tells a future maintainer exactly which invariants are *not* here and who holds them. ✔

